        "answer": {
          "short": null,
          "worked": "From part a, $f(x)=1-\\dfrac{2}{x+1}$. For $x\\ge0$, the graph starts at $(0,-1)$, crosses the $x$-axis at $(1,0)$ and rises towards $y=1$ from below. Keep this right-hand portion and reflect it across the $y$-axis. The reflected intercept is $(-1,0)$, and the two portions meet at a pointed minimum $(0,-1)$. Since $|x|+1>0$, the domain is $\\mathbb{R}$ and the range is $[-1,1)$.",
